 \section{Verification tests and failure boundaries}
 A deterministic standard-library harness tested 50,000 seeded rational cases and exact boundary witnesses. It also retained two negative controls. Without normalization, weights $(1,1,1)$ amplify a common $\varepsilon$ shift to $3\varepsilon$. Without nonnegativity, weights $(2,-1,0)$ sum to one but an adversarial signed component shift produces $3\varepsilon$. These are assumption failures, not exceptions to the proposition.
 
