 \section{Discussion, limitations, and falsifiable use}
 The envelope is useful only when component semantics, scales, and reference times are already aligned. It says nothing about whether the reference is true, whether the weights are legitimate, whether the three components are sufficient, or whether uncertainty is correlated or distributional. Run 118's temporal-coherence problem remains separate, as does Run 132's governance problem for changing weights.
